@startuml Email Preferences Flow - Clubinho NIB API
!theme plain
hide footbox

title E-mail preferences — public unsubscribe and signed-in settings

actor Recipient
actor "Signed-in user" as User
participant EmailPreferencesController as Controller
participant GetEmailPreferencesService as GetService
participant UpdateEmailPreferencesService as Service
participant UnsubscribeTokenService as Token
database "MySQL\nUserRepository" as Database

Recipient -> Controller : POST /email-preferences/unsubscribe { token }
Controller -> Service : unsubscribeFromNotices(token)
Service -> Token : verify signed token
Token --> Service : user id or invalid

alt Invalid token or unknown user
  Service --> Recipient : 422 same generic error
else Known user
  Service -> Database : find user; set noticesUnsubscribedAt once
  Service --> Recipient : 200 unsubscribed=true
end

note over Recipient, Database
  The token is the only credential. The operation is idempotent
  and never reveals whether an account exists.
end note

== Notification settings (JWT) ==

User -> Controller : GET /email-preferences/me
Controller -> GetService : findMine(userId)
GetService -> Database : find user
GetService --> User : 200 { noticesEnabled: !noticesUnsubscribedAt }

User -> Controller : PUT /email-preferences/me { noticesEnabled }
Controller -> Service : updateMine(userId, noticesEnabled)
Service -> Database : find user
alt noticesEnabled = false
  Service -> Database : keep or set noticesUnsubscribedAt
else noticesEnabled = true
  Service -> Database : clear noticesUnsubscribedAt
end
Service --> User : 200 { noticesEnabled }

note over User, Database
  Same field as the footer link: bulk notices (week material, events,
  informatives, documents, club reminders) skip users with a date.
  Account and security e-mails are always sent.
end note

@enduml
